ched by label or alias; the band 'Metallica' plus a moth genus that is a bare taxon) with made-up item IDs (Q9003xx). 'heat' is made up in the same shape (the kind item 'heat' with a P279, then the basketball team 'Miami Heat' matching through its 'Heat' alias; Q90033x): a sports team that loses the pick to a kind item. Moose, shredder, hulk and the napoleon pastry (#186, D-51) are made-up item IDs copying the shape of the live search: a person 'Moose' before the animal labelled 'moose'; the character 'Shredder' before kinds that match only through the alias 'shredder' ('paper shredder', 'grater'); the character 'Hulk' before a ship type labelled 'hulk'; 'Napoleon' before the pastry 'mille-feuille' (alias 'napoleon'). 'kraken' (#185) uses real IDs and the live search order of 2026-11-15 (the band Kraken, the Kraken cryptocurrency exchange, a film, a genus that is a bare taxon, then a website), with the class walk cut short: the band loses the pick but still blocks capitalized 'Kraken'. 'chicago bulls', 'philadelphia eagles', 'wolf' and 'yankees' (#310) use real IDs and the live search order of 2026-11-15, with the class walk cut short: the Chicago Bulls basketball team before a defunct American football team of the same name; the Philadelphia Eagles before an article on their history; five other items before the grey wolf (result 6, with the family name 'Wolf' first); and for 'yankees' the item 'Americans' first, the New York Yankees second (through their 'Yankees' alias), then the United States, and the kinds 'Yankee' and 'Northerners' (both alias 'Yankees'), so the team loses the pick to a kind item and its alias has no 'The' of its own (the 'heat' shape; docs/safety.md, known limits). 'search' maps a lowercased name to wbsearchentities-style results ('match' = the text that matched); 'default' is the reply for any other name (no match). 'entities' holds P31 (instance of) and P279 (subclass of).",
